{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>On the tenth day of the month, the mountaintops were seen.</b> Now Noah fixed [the date as] the first of the month though he did not see the moon, for he had not yet opened the window of the ark. And on the tenth of the month of Shevat he sent the raven, and it kept going and returning until Noah went out, for so it says, \"until the waters dried up,\" and on the day the earth dried Noah went out with all who were with him. And after seven days from when he sent the raven he sent the dove, and this was on the seventeenth of Shevat, which is the tenth month from the day of the Flood. Now this accords with the quadruple reckoning, and the proof is what it says: \"He waited again another seven days.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:45.923112898Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}